--- Combinatorial Designs (H06-H10) ---

H06: Steiner S(2,3,7): blocks=7 vs n+1=7
  S(2,3,7) blocks = 7
  n+1 = 6+1 = 7
  Match: True  🟩 EXACT
  Note: Fano plane IS S(2,3,7). blocks = points = 7 = n+1 (n=6)

H07: Kirkman schoolgirl: 15=C(6,2) girls in groups of 3
  C(6,2) = 15  (= number of girls)
  Rounds = (15-1)/(3-1) = 7  vs n+1=7  MATCH
  Groups per round = 15/3 = 5  vs TAU6+1=5
  🟩 EXACT  15=C(6,2) exact match

H08: Latin squares order 6: count factors through 6!?
  Reduced LS(6) = 9408
  Total LS(6)   = 812,851,200
  = 9408 * 6! * 5! = 9408 * 720 * 120
  9408 = 2 * 2 * 2 * 2 * 2 * 2 * 3 * 7 * 7 (= 2^7 * 3 * 5^? * ...)
  2^7=128, 9408/128=73.5000
  9408 = 2^7 * 73.5? No. Check: 9408 = 2^6 * 147 = 2^6 * 3 * 49 = 2^6 * 3 * 7^2
  Verify: 64 * 3 * 49 = 9408
  total_ls6 mod 6! = 0  (0 = divisible by 6!)
  🟩 EXACT: total LS(6) is divisible by 6!

H09: BIBD(6,3,2): does it exist? b=10, r=5, lambda=2
  v=6, k=3, lambda=2
  b = lambda*v*(v-1)/(k*(k-1)) = 10.0000  -> 10 blocks
  r = lambda*(v-1)/(k-1)       = 5.0000  -> 5 reps
  Existence (integers): True
  b = 10 = sigma(6) - 2 = 10? YES
  b = 10 = TAU6+6 = 10? YES
  r = 5 = PHI6+3 = 5? No, r=5=P6-6=5
  BIBD(6,3,2) EXISTS with b=10, r=5  🟩 EXACT

H10: Fano plane automorphism group |Aut(PG(2,2))| = 168 = 6*28?
  |Aut(Fano)| = 168
  6 * 28 = 168  MATCH
  Also: 168 = 8 * 21 = 8 * C(7,2) = 8 * 21
  168 = 2^3 * 3 * 7 = TAU6! * 7 = 24 * 7 = 168
  6*28=168  🟩 EXACT

