--- KEY INSIGHTS (Mission 1: x^x cluster analysis) ---
  The x^x ≈ ln(2) cluster is GEOMETRIC, not structural:
  • min(x^x) = e^(-1/e) = 0.692201  vs  ln(2) = 0.693147
  • Gap = 0.000947 ≈ 1/1000 — small but NOT analytically clean
  • All GZ reciprocals fall within ln(4/3)=0.288 of the minimum x=1/e
  • Flatness of x^x near minimum creates the 'cluster'
  • This is a CURVATURE phenomenon, not a GZ/n=6 structural identity
